{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"voice-creation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voice Creation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every text-to-speech provider ships a fixed catalog of voices. Your narrator, your character, or your brand can be absent from that catalog. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVoice()"},{"type":"text","value":" makes a new voice instead of picking one."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are two ways to create a voice:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Design"}]},{"type":"text","value":": you describe the voice in words. The provider invents it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clone"}]},{"type":"text","value":": you supply a clip of a real speaker, and the provider derives a\nvoice from it."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both give you a voice ID. Pass that ID to "},{"type":"link","href":"./text-to-speech","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" as the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voice"},{"type":"text","value":" option."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"design-a-voice-from-a-description","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Design a voice from a description"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Describe the voice you want. The provider returns candidate voices, each with a short preview you can listen to."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateVoice } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst result = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign('eleven_ttv_v3'),\n  prompt: 'A warm, gravelly narrator in his sixties with a slight Irish lilt',\n})\n\nfor (const voice of result.voices) {\n  console.log(voice.voiceId) // Pass this to generateSpeech()\n  console.log(voice.audio) // Base64 preview audio\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A longer, more specific description gives a better result. Name the age, the accent, the pace, and the mood."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"speak-with-the-new-voice","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Speak with the new voice"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The voice ID goes straight into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech, generateVoice } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech, elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst designed = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign('eleven_ttv_v3'),\n  prompt: 'A warm, gravelly narrator in his sixties',\n})\n\nconst [best] = designed.voices\nif (!best) throw new Error('The provider returned no voices.')\n\nconst speech = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech('eleven_v4'),\n  text: 'Once upon a time, in a village at the edge of the sea...',\n  voice: best.voiceId,\n})\n\nconsole.log(speech.contentType) // 'audio/mpeg'","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keep-a-voice-for-later","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep a voice for later"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A designed voice is a preview by default. Previews expire. To keep a voice in the provider's library, pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateVoice } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst result = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign('eleven_ttv_v3'),\n  prompt: 'A bright, upbeat product demo host',\n  name: 'Demo Host',\n  description: 'Bright, upbeat, mid-30s',\n})\n\nconst [saved] = result.voices\nif (!saved) throw new Error('The provider returned no voices.')\n\nconsole.log(saved.saved) // true\nconsole.log(saved.voiceId) // A permanent voice ID. Store it.","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Store "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voiceId"},{"type":"text","value":" in your database. Every later "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech()"},{"type":"text","value":" call reuses it, and you never design the same voice twice."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providers differ on what "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" means. ElevenLabs keeps a voice only when you give a name. Read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"saved"},{"type":"text","value":" on each returned voice to see what happened."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"guide-a-design-with-reference-audio","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guide a design with reference audio"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some models take a clip of a real speaker as a reference. Pass the audio as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"referenceAudio"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs is a design-with-reference, not a straight copy: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_ttv_v3"},{"type":"text","value":"\nstill needs a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.promptStrength"},{"type":"text","value":" sets how much of the\nresult comes from the description rather than the clip. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" for a result\nthat leans almost entirely on the reference."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises'\nimport { generateVoice } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst clip = await readFile('./narrator.mp3')\n\nconst result = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign('eleven_ttv_v3'),\n  prompt: 'The same speaker, but younger and more energetic',\n  // `new Blob([clip])`, not `clip.buffer`: a Buffer can be a view into a\n  // shared pool, so its `.buffer` is not necessarily just the file's bytes.\n  referenceAudio: new Blob([clip]),\n  name: 'Young Narrator',\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"referenceAudio"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts a base64 string, a base64 data URL, a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Blob"},{"type":"text","value":", a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"File"},{"type":"text","value":", or an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ArrayBuffer"},{"type":"text","value":". A remote URL is refused: read the file yourself and pass the bytes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CAUTION: Clone a voice only with the consent of the speaker. Most providers make this a condition of their terms."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"find-a-voice-you-made-earlier","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Find a voice you made earlier"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Store the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voiceId"},{"type":"text","value":" and you never need this. If you lose it, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listVoices()"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the account's catalog back."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { listVoices } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst { voices } = await listVoices({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech('eleven_v4'),\n  origins: ['generated', 'cloned'],\n})\n\nfor (const voice of voices) {\n  console.log(voice.voiceId, voice.name)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each voice carries "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voiceId"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"description"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"previewUrl"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"labels"},{"type":"text","value":" when the provider reports them. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin"},{"type":"text","value":" is one of:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"premade"},{"type":"text","value":": the provider's stock catalog."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generated"},{"type":"text","value":": designed from a description."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cloned"},{"type":"text","value":": made from reference audio."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"professional"},{"type":"text","value":": a curated or paid tier."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Leave "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origins"},{"type":"text","value":" off to get everything, including the stock voices."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only providers with a per-account catalog implement this. Where the voice list is fixed, the provider package publishes it instead, which is better than a network call: use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GeminiTTSVoices"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-gemini"},{"type":"text","value":", or the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OpenAITTSVoice"},{"type":"text","value":" union from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openai"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listVoices()"},{"type":"text","value":" throws on those adapters, and the message points at those exports."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"provider-support","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider support"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Design"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reference audio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes, on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eleven_ttv_v3"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsVoiceDesign()"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs is the only provider with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVoice()"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter today."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providers such as OpenAI, Gemini, and Cloudflare have a fixed voice catalog. They have no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVoice()"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter, and they will not get one."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"xAI, BytePlus, and fal.ai each publish a voice-cloning API, so they are the\ncandidates for the next adapter. None is implemented here yet, and this page\nwill describe them once one is."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VoiceAdapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The voice adapter, created with a model."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A text description of the voice."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"referenceAudio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string | File | Blob | ArrayBuffer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A clip of the speaker to clone."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The name to store the voice under."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"description"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A description stored with the voice."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"object"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider-specific options, typed per adapter."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You must give "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"referenceAudio"},{"type":"text","value":", or both. ElevenLabs always needs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":", because its design endpoint requires a description."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each returned voice carries "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voiceId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"saved"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":", plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audio"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"contentType"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"language"},{"type":"text","value":" when the provider reports them. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'ready'"},{"type":"text","value":" on every adapter today, because they all finish the voice before returning."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./text-to-speech","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text-to-Speech"}]},{"type":"text","value":": speak with the voice you made."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/elevenlabs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": model IDs and provider options."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"voice-creation","text":"Voice Creation","level":1},{"id":"design-a-voice-from-a-description","text":"Design a voice from a description","level":2},{"id":"speak-with-the-new-voice","text":"Speak with the new voice","level":2},{"id":"keep-a-voice-for-later","text":"Keep a voice for later","level":2},{"id":"guide-a-design-with-reference-audio","text":"Guide a design with reference audio","level":2},{"id":"find-a-voice-you-made-earlier","text":"Find a voice you made earlier","level":2},{"id":"provider-support","text":"Provider support","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Voice Creation\n\nEvery text-to-speech provider ships a fixed catalog of voices. Your narrator, your character, or your brand can be absent from that catalog. `generateVoice()` makes a new voice instead of picking one.\n\nThere are two ways to create a voice:\n\n- **Design**: you describe the voice in words. The provider invents it.\n- **Clone**: you supply a clip of a real speaker, and the provider derives a\n  voice from it.\n\nBoth give you a voice ID. Pass that ID to [`generateSpeech()`](./text-to-speech) as the `voice` option.\n\n## Design a voice from a description\n\nDescribe the voice you want. The provider returns candidate voices, each with a short preview you can listen to.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVoice } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst result = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign('eleven_ttv_v3'),\n  prompt: 'A warm, gravelly narrator in his sixties with a slight Irish lilt',\n})\n\nfor (const voice of result.voices) {\n  console.log(voice.voiceId) // Pass this to generateSpeech()\n  console.log(voice.audio) // Base64 preview audio\n}\n```\n\nA longer, more specific description gives a better result. Name the age, the accent, the pace, and the mood.\n\n## Speak with the new voice\n\nThe voice ID goes straight into `generateSpeech()`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech, generateVoice } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech, elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst designed = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign('eleven_ttv_v3'),\n  prompt: 'A warm, gravelly narrator in his sixties',\n})\n\nconst [best] = designed.voices\nif (!best) throw new Error('The provider returned no voices.')\n\nconst speech = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech('eleven_v4'),\n  text: 'Once upon a time, in a village at the edge of the sea...',\n  voice: best.voiceId,\n})\n\nconsole.log(speech.contentType) // 'audio/mpeg'\n```\n\n## Keep a voice for later\n\nA designed voice is a preview by default. Previews expire. To keep a voice in the provider's library, pass a `name`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVoice } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst result = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign('eleven_ttv_v3'),\n  prompt: 'A bright, upbeat product demo host',\n  name: 'Demo Host',\n  description: 'Bright, upbeat, mid-30s',\n})\n\nconst [saved] = result.voices\nif (!saved) throw new Error('The provider returned no voices.')\n\nconsole.log(saved.saved) // true\nconsole.log(saved.voiceId) // A permanent voice ID. Store it.\n```\n\nStore `voiceId` in your database. Every later `generateSpeech()` call reuses it, and you never design the same voice twice.\n\nProviders differ on what `name` means. ElevenLabs keeps a voice only when you give a name. Read `saved` on each returned voice to see what happened.\n\n## Guide a design with reference audio\n\nSome models take a clip of a real speaker as a reference. Pass the audio as\n`referenceAudio`.\n\nElevenLabs is a design-with-reference, not a straight copy: `eleven_ttv_v3`\nstill needs a `prompt`, and `modelOptions.promptStrength` sets how much of the\nresult comes from the description rather than the clip. Pass `0` for a result\nthat leans almost entirely on the reference.\n\n```typescript\nimport { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises'\nimport { generateVoice } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst clip = await readFile('./narrator.mp3')\n\nconst result = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign('eleven_ttv_v3'),\n  prompt: 'The same speaker, but younger and more energetic',\n  // `new Blob([clip])`, not `clip.buffer`: a Buffer can be a view into a\n  // shared pool, so its `.buffer` is not necessarily just the file's bytes.\n  referenceAudio: new Blob([clip]),\n  name: 'Young Narrator',\n})\n```\n\n`referenceAudio` accepts a base64 string, a base64 data URL, a `Blob`, a `File`, or an `ArrayBuffer`. A remote URL is refused: read the file yourself and pass the bytes.\n\nCAUTION: Clone a voice only with the consent of the speaker. Most providers make this a condition of their terms.\n\n## Find a voice you made earlier\n\nStore the `voiceId` and you never need this. If you lose it, `listVoices()` reads the account's catalog back.\n\n```typescript\nimport { listVoices } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst { voices } = await listVoices({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech('eleven_v4'),\n  origins: ['generated', 'cloned'],\n})\n\nfor (const voice of voices) {\n  console.log(voice.voiceId, voice.name)\n}\n```\n\nEach voice carries `voiceId`, and `name`, `origin`, `description`, `previewUrl` and `labels` when the provider reports them. `origin` is one of:\n\n- `premade`: the provider's stock catalog.\n- `generated`: designed from a description.\n- `cloned`: made from reference audio.\n- `professional`: a curated or paid tier.\n\nLeave `origins` off to get everything, including the stock voices.\n\nOnly providers with a per-account catalog implement this. Where the voice list is fixed, the provider package publishes it instead, which is better than a network call: use `GeminiTTSVoices` from `@tanstack/ai-gemini`, or the `OpenAITTSVoice` union from `@tanstack/ai-openai`. `listVoices()` throws on those adapters, and the message points at those exports.\n\n## Provider support\n\n| Provider | Design | Reference audio | Adapter |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ElevenLabs | Yes | Yes, on `eleven_ttv_v3` | `elevenlabsVoiceDesign()` |\n\nElevenLabs is the only provider with a `generateVoice()` adapter today.\n\nProviders such as OpenAI, Gemini, and Cloudflare have a fixed voice catalog. They have no `generateVoice()` adapter, and they will not get one.\n\nxAI, BytePlus, and fal.ai each publish a voice-cloning API, so they are the\ncandidates for the next adapter. None is implemented here yet, and this page\nwill describe them once one is.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `adapter` | `VoiceAdapter` | The voice adapter, created with a model. |\n| `prompt` | `string` | A text description of the voice. |\n| `referenceAudio` | `string \\| File \\| Blob \\| ArrayBuffer` | A clip of the speaker to clone. |\n| `name` | `string` | The name to store the voice under. |\n| `description` | `string` | A description stored with the voice. |\n| `modelOptions` | `object` | Provider-specific options, typed per adapter. |\n\nYou must give `prompt`, or `referenceAudio`, or both. ElevenLabs always needs `prompt`, because its design endpoint requires a description.\n\nEach returned voice carries `voiceId`, `saved`, and `status`, plus `audio`, `format`, `contentType`, `duration`, and `language` when the provider reports them. `status` is `'ready'` on every adapter today, because they all finish the voice before returning.\n\n## Next steps\n\n- [Text-to-Speech](./text-to-speech): speak with the voice you made.\n- [ElevenLabs adapter](../adapters/elevenlabs): model IDs and provider options.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Voice Creation\nid: voice-creation\norder: 3.5\ndescription: \"Create a custom voice from a text description or a reference clip with TanStack AI's generateVoice() API, then speak with it through generateSpeech().\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - voice creation\n  - voice design\n  - voice cloning\n  - generateVoice\n  - elevenlabs voice design\n  - custom voice\n---\n\n# Voice Creation\n\nEvery text-to-speech provider ships a fixed catalog of voices. Your narrator, your character, or your brand can be absent from that catalog. `generateVoice()` makes a new voice instead of picking one.\n\nThere are two ways to create a voice:\n\n- **Design**: you describe the voice in words. The provider invents it.\n- **Clone**: you supply a clip of a real speaker, and the provider derives a\n  voice from it.\n\nBoth give you a voice ID. Pass that ID to [`generateSpeech()`](./text-to-speech) as the `voice` option.\n\n## Design a voice from a description\n\nDescribe the voice you want. The provider returns candidate voices, each with a short preview you can listen to.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVoice } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst result = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign('eleven_ttv_v3'),\n  prompt: 'A warm, gravelly narrator in his sixties with a slight Irish lilt',\n})\n\nfor (const voice of result.voices) {\n  console.log(voice.voiceId) // Pass this to generateSpeech()\n  console.log(voice.audio) // Base64 preview audio\n}\n```\n\nA longer, more specific description gives a better result. Name the age, the accent, the pace, and the mood.\n\n## Speak with the new voice\n\nThe voice ID goes straight into `generateSpeech()`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech, generateVoice } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech, elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst designed = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign('eleven_ttv_v3'),\n  prompt: 'A warm, gravelly narrator in his sixties',\n})\n\nconst [best] = designed.voices\nif (!best) throw new Error('The provider returned no voices.')\n\nconst speech = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech('eleven_v4'),\n  text: 'Once upon a time, in a village at the edge of the sea...',\n  voice: best.voiceId,\n})\n\nconsole.log(speech.contentType) // 'audio/mpeg'\n```\n\n## Keep a voice for later\n\nA designed voice is a preview by default. Previews expire. To keep a voice in the provider's library, pass a `name`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVoice } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst result = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign('eleven_ttv_v3'),\n  prompt: 'A bright, upbeat product demo host',\n  name: 'Demo Host',\n  description: 'Bright, upbeat, mid-30s',\n})\n\nconst [saved] = result.voices\nif (!saved) throw new Error('The provider returned no voices.')\n\nconsole.log(saved.saved) // true\nconsole.log(saved.voiceId) // A permanent voice ID. Store it.\n```\n\nStore `voiceId` in your database. Every later `generateSpeech()` call reuses it, and you never design the same voice twice.\n\nProviders differ on what `name` means. ElevenLabs keeps a voice only when you give a name. Read `saved` on each returned voice to see what happened.\n\n## Guide a design with reference audio\n\nSome models take a clip of a real speaker as a reference. Pass the audio as\n`referenceAudio`.\n\nElevenLabs is a design-with-reference, not a straight copy: `eleven_ttv_v3`\nstill needs a `prompt`, and `modelOptions.promptStrength` sets how much of the\nresult comes from the description rather than the clip. Pass `0` for a result\nthat leans almost entirely on the reference.\n\n```typescript\nimport { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises'\nimport { generateVoice } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsVoiceDesign } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst clip = await readFile('./narrator.mp3')\n\nconst result = await generateVoice({\n  adapter: elevenlabsVoiceDesign('eleven_ttv_v3'),\n  prompt: 'The same speaker, but younger and more energetic',\n  // `new Blob([clip])`, not `clip.buffer`: a Buffer can be a view into a\n  // shared pool, so its `.buffer` is not necessarily just the file's bytes.\n  referenceAudio: new Blob([clip]),\n  name: 'Young Narrator',\n})\n```\n\n`referenceAudio` accepts a base64 string, a base64 data URL, a `Blob`, a `File`, or an `ArrayBuffer`. A remote URL is refused: read the file yourself and pass the bytes.\n\nCAUTION: Clone a voice only with the consent of the speaker. Most providers make this a condition of their terms.\n\n## Find a voice you made earlier\n\nStore the `voiceId` and you never need this. If you lose it, `listVoices()` reads the account's catalog back.\n\n```typescript\nimport { listVoices } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst { voices } = await listVoices({\n  adapter: elevenlabsSpeech('eleven_v4'),\n  origins: ['generated', 'cloned'],\n})\n\nfor (const voice of voices) {\n  console.log(voice.voiceId, voice.name)\n}\n```\n\nEach voice carries `voiceId`, and `name`, `origin`, `description`, `previewUrl` and `labels` when the provider reports them. `origin` is one of:\n\n- `premade`: the provider's stock catalog.\n- `generated`: designed from a description.\n- `cloned`: made from reference audio.\n- `professional`: a curated or paid tier.\n\nLeave `origins` off to get everything, including the stock voices.\n\nOnly providers with a per-account catalog implement this. Where the voice list is fixed, the provider package publishes it instead, which is better than a network call: use `GeminiTTSVoices` from `@tanstack/ai-gemini`, or the `OpenAITTSVoice` union from `@tanstack/ai-openai`. `listVoices()` throws on those adapters, and the message points at those exports.\n\n## Provider support\n\n| Provider | Design | Reference audio | Adapter |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ElevenLabs | Yes | Yes, on `eleven_ttv_v3` | `elevenlabsVoiceDesign()` |\n\nElevenLabs is the only provider with a `generateVoice()` adapter today.\n\nProviders such as OpenAI, Gemini, and Cloudflare have a fixed voice catalog. They have no `generateVoice()` adapter, and they will not get one.\n\nxAI, BytePlus, and fal.ai each publish a voice-cloning API, so they are the\ncandidates for the next adapter. None is implemented here yet, and this page\nwill describe them once one is.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `adapter` | `VoiceAdapter` | The voice adapter, created with a model. |\n| `prompt` | `string` | A text description of the voice. |\n| `referenceAudio` | `string \\| File \\| Blob \\| ArrayBuffer` | A clip of the speaker to clone. |\n| `name` | `string` | The name to store the voice under. |\n| `description` | `string` | A description stored with the voice. |\n| `modelOptions` | `object` | Provider-specific options, typed per adapter. |\n\nYou must give `prompt`, or `referenceAudio`, or both. ElevenLabs always needs `prompt`, because its design endpoint requires a description.\n\nEach returned voice carries `voiceId`, `saved`, and `status`, plus `audio`, `format`, `contentType`, `duration`, and `language` when the provider reports them. `status` is `'ready'` on every adapter today, because they all finish the voice before returning.\n\n## Next steps\n\n- [Text-to-Speech](./text-to-speech): speak with the voice you made.\n- [ElevenLabs adapter](../adapters/elevenlabs): model IDs and provider options.\n"}
